  "conclusion": "The pipeline reduced the body stage consistently (part screen: body p50 96.5/64.3 ms baseline vs 59.6/58.0 ms with 1 MiB read-ahead) but never produced a repeatable scored throughput win across four alternating batches or a simultaneous two-server A/B. Measured against 433438f, the per-part p50 was already lower than RustFS's while throughput was lower, because Warp pays a synchronous CompleteMultipartUpload tail per 10-part upload. The code was reverted and not merged; the completion tail (later cut by the section-11 assembly pipeline) was the scored lever.",
